user.admin: Set up an admin account that logs in with an SSH key and uses sudo
  note: no `authorized_keys` given: copies 1 key from /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
  + create user admin                                                     partial
  + ~admin/.ssh/authorized_keys (mode 0600, admin:admin)                  reversible
      @@ -0,0 +1 @@
      +ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGroot root@laptop
  + /etc/sudoers.d/90-vps-ready-admin (mode 0440, root:root)              reversible
      @@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
